@namespace NSail.Components.Tests.Fixtures

@using NSail.Components
@using NSail.Icons

@* Calqued from WorkOrderPage's own footer: a secondary act with an icon (Collect), the
   hero with none (the common shape across the document pages today), and a secondary act
   with no icon at all (PurchaseOrderPage's Cancel/Issue/Receive) — the one combination the
   emphasis-ladder collapse must leave alone, nothing to collapse TO.

   SignOut is the second SHAPE of hero: the one act of its surface, destructive, so it wears
   Danger instead of Primary and carries a glyph. It is the case the collapse rule has to
   spare by emphasis rather than by colour. *@
<NsPanel>
    <Footer>
        <NsButton Icon="@NsIcons.Payments" Label="Collect" />
        <NsButton As="NsAs.Danger" Label="Cancel" />
        <NsButton As="NsAs.Danger" Breakpoint="NsBreakpoint.Always" Icon="@NsIcons.Logout" Label="SignOut" />
        <NsButton As="NsAs.Main" Label="Save" />
    </Footer>
</NsPanel>
